---
/* Strive Studio, told the same way as the Strive AI story: a short deck of
   numbered "slides", each a headline, two pointers and a picture. The journey
   in full lives in /writing/strive-studio-frontend/, linked from the big card
   at the end. */
import WorkLayout from '../../layouts/WorkLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import ReportBuilder from '../../components/sketches/ReportBuilder.astro';
import StudioGlance from '../../components/sketches/studio/StudioGlance.astro';
import Versus from '../../components/sketches/studio/Versus.astro';
import ShareInsightsSteps from '../../components/sketches/studio/ShareInsightsSteps.astro';
import TwoKindsOfUI from '../../components/sketches/studio/TwoKindsOfUI.astro';
import SandboxBridge from '../../components/sketches/studio/SandboxBridge.astro';
import DesignContext from '../../components/sketches/studio/DesignContext.astro';
import StudioToChat from '../../components/sketches/studio/StudioToChat.astro';

const description = "Strive Studio: describe a marketing report in chat and get back a live dashboard wired to your own data. How we let the agent write the report as HTML, host it safely in a sandbox, and fold it into the main chat, told from the frontend side.";

const lessons = [
  { miss: 'Wrote 650 lines of CSS for the agent to learn.', lesson: 'Give it taste, not a stylesheet. Extend what models already write, like Tailwind.' },
  { miss: 'Loaded every row on page load. Big accounts froze the tab.', lesson: 'Live should never mean heavy. Load what’s on screen, fetch the rest on demand.' },
  { miss: 'Early reports looked vibe-coded: four KPI cards in a row.', lesson: 'Brand context and emphasis rules make a report look like yours.' },
  { miss: 'Exported multi-page reports in one go.', lesson: 'Snapshot page by page, and put a hard cap on the size.' },
];
---
<WorkLayout
  title="Strive Studio — agent-written live reports"
  description={description}
  ogDescription="Describe a marketing report in chat, get back a live dashboard wired to your own data. The frontend side of Strive Studio."
  eyebrow="Strivelabs · Design engineer · 2026 → now"
  heading="Strive Studio"
  facts={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Design engineer · frontend' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'In production, still shipping' },
  ]}
  link={{ href: 'https://strivelabs.ai/', label: 'strivelabs.ai' }}
  schema={{
    name: 'Strive Studio — report builder',
    url: 'https://strivelabs.ai/',
    description: 'Describe a marketing report in chat and get back a live dashboard: agent-written HTML in a sandboxed iframe, live read-only data through a host bridge, and design context handed to the agent.',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    keywords: 'generative UI, AI reports, live dashboards, sandboxed iframe, postMessage, design systems, Tailwind, design engineering, UX for AI',
  }}
>
  <ReportBuilder slot="sketch" />

  <Fragment slot="lede">Describe a marketing report in chat and get back a <mark class="hl">live dashboard</mark>, wired to your own ad and CRM data. Think Lovable for marketing, or Claude artifacts whose numbers never go stale. We built it as a small team; this is the frontend side.</Fragment>

  <div class="story">
    <StudioGlance />

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-back">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Backstory</p><h2 id="s-back">It started with insights</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li><a href="/work/strive-gen-ui-chat/">Strive AI</a> could already turn a chat into a shareable <strong>insight doc</strong>: blocks you pick, plus AI summaries.</li>
        <li>It still lives on as <code>/share-insights</code>. But reports wanted more: <strong>live data, big volumes, and a story you get in one scan.</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <ShareInsightsSteps only="result" caption="v1, still in the product: blocks from a chat, compiled into an insight doc beside the thread." />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-bet">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">The bet</p><h2 id="s-bet">Let the model write HTML</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>Every new report layout meant <strong>another schema and another UI tool</strong>. Some reports can’t be written as JSON at all.</li>
        <li>So for reports we dropped schemas, and let the agent write what it knows best.</li>
      </ul>
      <aside class="qa sk-box sk-lean-2" aria-label="Where the idea came from">
        <div class="qa-row">
          <span class="qa-av" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          <p class="qa-bubble"><span>Our CTO</span>“What if we just let the agent write the code, instead of struggling with schemas and teaching it to make sense of them?”</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
      <TwoKindsOfUI />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-name">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Design call · naming</p><h2 id="s-name">Two ways to share, one product</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>We couldn’t drop insights. Snapshots with AI summaries, on a schedule, and <strong>customers liked them.</strong></li>
        <li>So I named the two apart, and gave reports a studio and a home of their own.</li>
      </ul>
      <Versus
        left={{ title: '/share-insights · insight doc', tone: 'teal', items: ['A snapshot of one moment in a chat', 'The chat’s blocks, plus AI summaries', 'Re-run on a schedule for a fresh copy'] }}
        right={{ title: 'Report Studio · live report', stamp: 'live', tone: 'coral', items: ['A dashboard on your connected data', 'Agent-written HTML, laid out your way', 'Its own Reports page, linked to chat'] }}
        mid="&"
        marks="dot"
        alt="Two ways to share. The share-insights skill makes an insight doc: a snapshot of one moment in a chat, the chat’s blocks plus AI summaries, re-run on a schedule. Report Studio makes a live report: a dashboard on your connected data, agent-written HTML laid out your way, with its own Reports page linked to chat."
        caption="Insights for a moment worth keeping; reports for numbers that keep moving."
      />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-safe">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Security</p><h2 id="s-safe">Untrusted HTML, trusted data</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>The report runs in a <strong>sandboxed iframe</strong>: no cookies, no storage, no direct line to our API.</li>
        <li>It <strong>asks the host</strong> for data. The host checks every message, holds the credentials, and only runs read-only calls.</li>
      </ul>
      <SandboxBridge caption="The report can ask for anything. It can’t hold anything." />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-design">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Design context</p><h2 id="s-design">From a stylesheet to a little taste</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>I first wrote <strong>650 lines of CSS</strong> for the agent to learn. It didn’t scale, and fought the point of dropping schemas.</li>
        <li>Now it’s <strong>a little taste plus Tailwind</strong>, which models already write fluently, and brand context pulled in at onboarding.</li>
      </ul>
      <DesignContext />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-data">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Scale</p><h2 id="s-data">Live, not heavy</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li>Loading every row on page load <strong>froze the tab</strong> on big accounts.</li>
        <li>Now reports load what you see first, and <strong>query the rest on demand</strong>, paginated on both ends.</li>
      </ul>
      <Versus
        left={{ title: 'Before · everything at once', tone: 'ghost', items: ['Every row fetched on page load', 'The tab stalls on big accounts', 'Heavy pages break'] }}
        right={{ title: 'Now · progressive loading', stamp: 'lazy', tone: 'teal', items: ['What you see loads first', 'Queries run as you scroll or switch tabs', 'Paginated on client and server'] }}
        alt="Before: every row fetched on page load, the tab stalls on big accounts and heavy pages break. Now, with progressive loading: what you see loads first, queries run as you scroll or switch tabs, and results are paginated on client and server."
        caption="Live should never mean heavy."
      />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-fold">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Shipping it</p><h2 id="s-fold">Build apart, then fold in</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="doodle-list slide-points">
        <li><strong>v1 was its own chat</strong>, to keep report rules out of the main prompt and experiment undisturbed. The price: a separate history.</li>
        <li><strong>v2 made it a skill</strong> in the main chat, with the report in a canvas beside the thread. One chat, one history.</li>
      </ul>
      <StudioToChat />
    </section>

    <section class="slide" aria-labelledby="s-lessons">
      <header class="slide-head">
        <span class="slide-num" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
        <div><p class="slide-kicker">Misses &amp; lessons</p><h2 id="s-lessons">What the first reports taught us</h2></div>
      </header>
      <ul class="lessons">
        {lessons.map((l, i) => (
          <li class:list={['sk-box', `sk-lean-${i + 1}`]}>
            <p class="lessons-miss"><span>Miss</span>{l.miss}</p>
            <p class="lessons-learn"><span>Lesson</span>{l.lesson}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <blockquote class="closer">A dashboard shows you numbers someone else chose. This builds the report you asked for, and keeps it alive.</blockquote>

    <a class="deep-dive wobbly wobbly--2" href="/writing/strive-studio-frontend/">
      <span class="deep-dive-shot taped ink-shot">
        <img src="/images/writing/strive-studio/sketch-studio-flow.webp" alt="" width="2400" height="1888" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      </span>
      <span class="deep-dive-body">
        <span class="deep-dive-eyebrow"><Icon name="pen" />Deep dive · ~10 min read</span>
        <strong>Building live reports inside Strive: the story of Strive Studio</strong>
        <span class="deep-dive-sub">The backstory, the naming call, the bet on HTML, and everything that broke at scale.</span>
        <span class="deep-dive-go">Read the full story<Icon name="arrow-right" /></span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

</WorkLayout>

<style>
  /* Same deck styles as the Strive AI story. The story runs the full width of
     the narrow wrap; only the pointers keep a reading measure. */
  :global(.prose:has(> .story)) { max-width: none; }
  .story :global(.sk-fig) { margin: var(--space-3) 0 0; }

  .slide { margin-top: var(--space-5); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: 1.5px dashed var(--line); }
  .slide-head { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .slide-num { flex: none; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 6vw, 3.8rem); line-height: .85; color: var(--coral); }
  .slide:nth-of-type(2n) .slide-num { color: var(--blue); }
  .slide:nth-of-type(3n) .slide-num { color: var(--teal); }
  .slide-kicker { margin: 0 0 .3rem !important; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .prose .slide-head h2 { margin: 0; }
  .slide-points { max-width: 60ch; }
  .slide-points li { font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .slide-points strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }

  /* The CTO line, as a chat message with an avatar, like the "Claude copy?"
     exchange on the Strive AI story. A drawn face stands in for a photo. */
  .qa { margin-top: var(--space-3); padding: 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.2rem; }
  .qa-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: .65rem; }
  .qa-bubble { margin: 0 !important; max-width: min(36rem, 100%); padding: .6rem .85rem .7rem; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink) !important; background: var(--sand); border: 1.5px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px 14px 14px 4px; }
  .qa-bubble span { display: block; margin-bottom: .15rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .6rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--teal); }
  .qa-av { position: relative; flex: none; width: 2.4rem; height: 2.4rem; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 50%; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: var(--sand-2); }
  .qa-av i { position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: -.45rem; width: 1.5rem; height: 1.9rem; transform: translateX(-50%); border-radius: 50% 50% 40% 40%; border: 1.5px solid var(--ink); background: var(--teal); }

  .lessons { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.2rem; }
  .lessons li { display: grid; gap: .55rem; align-content: start; padding: .9rem 1rem 1rem; }
  .lessons p { margin: 0 !important; max-width: none; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .lessons span { display: block; margin-bottom: .1rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lessons-miss { color: var(--ink-faint) !important; }
  .lessons-miss span { color: var(--coral); }
  .lessons-learn { color: var(--ink) !important; font-weight: 500; }
  .lessons-learn span { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 400; }
  @media (max-width: 559px) { .lessons { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .closer { margin-top: var(--space-5); }

  /* The big card to the long-form write-up. */
  .deep-dive { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-4); padding: 1.2rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); box-shadow: 4px 5px 0 var(--shadow-ink); transition: transform .2s ease, box-shadow .2s ease; }
  .deep-dive:hover { color: var(--ink); transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 6px 8px 0 var(--shadow-ink); }
  .deep-dive-shot { display: block; aspect-ratio: 16 / 7; overflow: visible; border: 1.5px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px 5px 12px 6px / 6px 12px 5px 10px; background: #fff; transform: rotate(-.6deg); transition: transform .25s ease; }
  .deep-dive:hover .deep-dive-shot { transform: rotate(0); }
  .deep-dive-shot img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 92%; border-radius: inherit; }
  .deep-dive-body { display: grid; gap: .45rem; padding: 1.2rem .3rem .2rem; }
  .deep-dive-eyebrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .45rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .deep-dive-eyebrow :global(.doodle) { color: var(--coral); width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; }
  .deep-dive strong { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2vw, 2.1rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .deep-dive-sub { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .deep-dive-go { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem; margin-top: .3rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--coral); }
  .deep-dive-go :global(.doodle) { width: 1rem; height: 1rem; stroke-width: 2; transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .deep-dive:hover .deep-dive-go :global(.doodle) { transform: translateX(4px); }
</style>
